    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29585" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσφημ-ία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ill language</i>, esp. <i>words
				of ill omen</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατεῖχε . . πᾶν στρατόπεδον δυσφημίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				16.4.1
			</span></i>: pl., <i>curses</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.587f
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pel.</u>
				8
			</span></i>; but, <i>unsavoury details</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				302
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>blasphemy, slander</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				6.48
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>ill fame, obloquy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				178
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				7.99c
			</span></i>.</div>
